-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Three Weeks in Paradise
  Publisher   Mikro-Gen, 1986
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Three Weeks in Paradise (1986)(Mikro-Gen)(128K).z80
  MD5         bf0eff8438e543f18e76d14940665d7d

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Wally and the other characters in the fuller colours of an older
              Spec256 conversion. Source: Enhanced colours from the MVV
              package's older Spec256 conversion, painter not established.

  Pace        original (+0.46% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless on the
              NextZXOS v2.09 card, against the plain build of the same start
              state; probe 0xA8ED, keys keyed to updates, game state equal at
              every update)

  Changes     1.1: works on NextZXOS v2.10 (System/Next 26.11); the hooks hand
              back the CPU speed the game was running at; the pace code is now
              NexClash's shared library (pace as 1.0)

  Note        Scenery that Wally walks behind covers him as whole objects
              (plants, palms), with the right-edge palms in front. Plays at
              the original's pace: the hooks are timed so the patch costs no
              speed (1.1 measured +0.46% and +0.16% over 600 game updates,
              Enhanced +0.42% and +0.37%, in JNext, 2026-11-07). The slowdown
              in busy rooms and the music lagging while an effect plays are
              the original game's own: its tune and effects share the beeper.
              Works on NextZXOS v2.10 from 1.1. Known issues: the pace evens
              out over a few updates: the slowest 20-update stretch in each
              run was about 7% behind the original, as in 1.0. Missing: the
              lives cheat was checked on the original code, not in this build;
              not reached in testing: the puzzles, Wilma, Herbert and the
              ending; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immune to enemies

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

